      },
      "text": "The simulation results presented in the next section reveal that this upper bound becomes tight as the SNR increases. This observation may be explained as follows. As the SNR increases, the events referred to on the right-hand side of (75) become nearly non-overlapping, equivalently, it will be unlikely that any pair of these events happen simultaneously. In that case, the inequality in (76) will become closer to an equality.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
