      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5097679738562092,
        "y0": 0.31554797979797977,
        "x1": 0.8412516339869281,
        "y1": 0.33056691919191916
      },
      "text": "C. Upper Bound for Quasi-Orthogonal Signaling",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5097679738562092,
        "y0": 0.3352436868686869,
        "x1": 0.9199934640522875,
        "y1": 0.425875
      },
      "text": "The desired bound here can be derived following those of the biorthogonal case with some minor modifications. First, for the case where M = 2, the decision boundary that separates s0 and s1 is the bisect line between them. This is the line in the direction d1 in Fig. 1(a). With this observation, the probability of a symbol error here is found to be",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
